{"ts": 1789784507.004879, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "Signs confirmed: all-positive dominates decisively for {2, 26, 31} (1.391 vs. 0.63/0.50/0.27 for flips), so these are genuine directional effects, not sign-fitting artifacts.\n\nThe control test is informative too. Adding the *best-looking noise* features to {2,26} gives ~1.12\u20131.24, all **below** the 1.236 of {2,26} alone. So the noise features add nothing \u2014 dilution slightly outweighs any spurious gain. Feature 31's lift (1.236 \u2192 1.391) is real signal, not a selection artifact.\n\nOne last check \u2014 I want to make sure 31 is the right third leg and see how much of 2's edge is robust."}
